Three identical 128 GB USB sticks on a Raspberry Pi 5. SYNTHETIC: written
from the shape of real lsblk and udevadm outputs, to be replaced by a capture
of the real sticks (tools/pi/collect.sh). sda and sdb report the same serial
number, as some cheap sticks do: udev gives both the same by-id name.

